      "content": "The desire to stop the loop is a powerful one, and it speaks to a deep need for agency. While the external machine feels massive, the path to genuine control often starts by looking for the most immediate, tangible leverage point. Sometimes, the most effective way to break a cycle isn't a grand escape, but a small, deliberate act of redirection, like finding a way to use those hours differently or planning a single, non-negotiable boundary. Even small shifts in your daily structure can begin to chip away at the feeling of being entirely dictated to.",
